{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Problem\n\nPlan review has two shortcuts that skip the billable LLM review on an unchanged ticket: `reuse.idempotent_reuse` (reuses a still-valid signed PASS) and `reuse.verdict_reuse` (reuses a stored BLOCK whose material fingerprint and code SHA still match). Both are bypassed only by `force`. Both rely on the material fingerprint changing when `file_impact` changes.\n\nExisting tests prove a full re-review after a **description** edit (`tests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_plan_review_gate.py::test_material_change_reruns_the_llm`, `tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py::test_material_change_reruns_full_review`). No test does the same for a **`file_impact`** edit, the edit in the incident below. If `file_impact` dropped out of the fingerprint (`material_diff.material_basis`), both shortcuts would quietly hand back a result for the old plan and no test would fail.\n\nThe MCP `gate_status` handle carries two verdicts: the run's own `verdict` (PASS/BLOCK) and `durable`, the ticket's current signed-approval currency (`plan_review_status`). After a material edit, a run that BLOCKs leaves the earlier attestation in place, so `durable.verdict` reads `stale-material` with the old `signed_at` beside `verdict: BLOCK`. That pairing is by design (d80d), and an agent read it as a replayed stale result. Nothing pins that the run's verdict and the durable status stay separate fields.\n\nInvestigation (comment on this ticket, 2026-10-31) found no defect in either shortcut: the step-4 run did a fresh 14-chunk review and blocked on its own finding. The verdict flip between runs is filed as `sadistic-noir-bustard` (`5503-c37b-2a44-447c`). This ticket adds the missing regression coverage only; no `src/` change.\n\n## Approach\n\nAll tests go in `tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py`, which already has a temp-store `repo` fixture and a counting offline runner (`_CountingGateFake`) that BLOCKs on criterion F1.\n\n1. Give `_CountingGateFake` a constructor flag `block: bool = True`. With `block=False` it emits no Pass-1 findings, so the review PASSes and signs.\n2. `test_file_impact_edit_bypasses_idempotent_reuse`: `set_file_impact` with one path, review with `block=False` (signed PASS). Widen `file_impact` to two paths. Review again without `force`. Assert the runner call count rose, `coverage.idempotent_skip` is not true, and `plan_review_status` is `certified` again.\n3. `test_file_impact_edit_bypasses_verdict_reuse`: blocked ticket with one-path `file_impact`, BLOCK review. Widen `file_impact`. Review again without `force`. Assert the call count rose and `coverage.verdict_reuse` is not true.\n4. `test_gate_status_keeps_run_verdict_apart_from_stale_attestation`: sign a PASS with one path, widen `file_impact`, then start a review through the MCP `review_plan_start` tool with `rebar.llm.review_plan` bound to the real review and the BLOCK runner. Poll `gate_run_status(job_id)` to terminal. Assert `status == \"passed\"`, `verdict == \"BLOCK\"`, `durable.verdict == \"stale-material\"` with the first attestation's `signed_at`, and `findings.readable` is true (the job's own sidecar).\n5. Mutation proof (not committed): drop `\"file_impact\"` from `material_basis`, confirm tests 2 and 3 fail, restore.\n\n## Files\n\n- `tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py` — runner flag + 3 tests.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] `pytest tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py` passes, including `test_file_impact_edit_bypasses_idempotent_reuse`, `test_file_impact_edit_bypasses_verdict_reuse`, and `test_gate_status_keeps_run_verdict_apart_from_stale_attestation`.\n- [ ] With `\"file_impact\"` removed from `material_basis` in `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/material_diff.py`, the two `file_impact_edit` tests fail; restored, they pass. Recorded in a comment on this ticket.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0.\n- [ ] `git diff origin/main --stat` lists only `tests/unit/test_plan_review_reuse.py`.\n\n## Testing\n\nOffline runner and a real temp store only; no LLM spend. Commands: the AC pytest line, the mutation run, `make lint`, `make typecheck`.","title":"Pin file_impact-edit re-review through both reuse shortcuts and gate_status verdict separation"}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793496102632387001,"uuid":"391c036b-ba06-4897-b27f-d5710052d128"}